 To achieve this task, you can use the following steps:

1. First, retrieve the content of the existing document (let's assume it is named 'hawaii-packing-list.docx').
2. Append the new packing list content to the existing one.
3. Create a new file with the name 'hawaii-packaging-list.docx' containing the combined content.
4. Share the newly created file with john.doe@gmail.com with read permissions.

Here is the code for these steps:

```json
{
  "name": "create_hawaii_packing_list",
  "arguments": {
    "existing_file_id": "<ID of the existing packing list file>",
    "new_content": "<The new packing list content>"
  },
  "function": {
    "name": "search_files_by_filename",
    "arguments": {
      "filename": "hawaii-packaging-list.docx"
    }
  },
  "then": {
    "name": "append_to_file",
    "arguments": {
      "content": "<The new packing list content>",
      "file_id": "$returnValue.file_id"
    }
  },
  "then": {
    "name": "create_file",
    "arguments": {
      "filename": "hawaii-packaging-list.docx",
      "content": "$returnValue.content"
    }
  },
  "then": {
    "name": "share_file",
    "arguments": {
      "email": "john.doe@gmail.com",
      "file_id": "$returnValue.file_id",
      "permission": "r"
    }
  }
}
```
